<title>USA: Star Technologies Q2 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Star Technologies Q2 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>STERLING, Va. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>					    Three Months  Six Months</p>
<p>				     Ended Sept. 30,  Ended Sept. 30,</p>
<p>					1996     1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Revenue			    $217     $505     $932   $3,081</p>
<p> Operating Loss		(1,374)  (1,113)  (2,026)  (1,584)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)	     5,180    (964)    4,589  (1,298)</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) applicable</p>
<p>   ro Common Shares	   15,561  (1,312)   14,622    3,010</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) per Common</p>
<p>and Common Equivalent Share</p>
<p>					 .78    (.07)	.74	.15</p>
<p>Average Shares Outstanding</p>
<p>				    19,878   19,880   19,884   19,877</p>
<p>NOTE: Income for the quarter and six months rose as a result of a successful breach-of-contract suit, which Star brought against General Electric Medical Systems. The suit was settled in the second quarter when Star received $9.4 million from GEMS.</p>
</text>
